                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9124175b-87e7-4b6f-a911-ed9fc3f6b235",
                        "source_entry_id": "23ac8405-09c0-3fff-b8a9-7e7c9e7c2aac",
                        "source_sense_id": "d1df6828-d7b7-3b27-b600-38c1b253e74a",
                        "source_sense_description": "een Noord-Amerikaans indianenschoeisel",
                        "target_lang_word": "Mokassin",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Mokassin",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e866ef95-cb4c-3f26-9eec-c1bb07c83545",
                                        "entry_id": "a17c79c3-73a2-34f7-a2a9-def90613cba6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "weicher, lederner Schuh ohne Absatz"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ac01af7-7e69-4dc8-8eb7-4b6d3ddf327f",
                                                "sense_id": "e866ef95-cb4c-3f26-9eec-c1bb07c83545",
                                                "text": "„Er trägt einen weißen Rollkragenpulli unter seinem blauen Sakko, sie einen beige karierten Trenchcoat über einem gemusterten Kleidchen, dazu die hellbraune Mokassins, natürlich von Gucci.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "468060df-4446-4c7b-9d5d-2f74fdbf7e94",
                                                "sense_id": "e866ef95-cb4c-3f26-9eec-c1bb07c83545",
                                                "text": "„Delgado bekam den Reiter an einem Mokassin und am Leibgurt zu fassen und riss ihn vom Pferd.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b591cb8-7a61-4cd0-be04-7af8fdfd8599",
                                                "sense_id": "e866ef95-cb4c-3f26-9eec-c1bb07c83545",
                                                "text": "„Die Spur war durch einen indianischen Mokassin verursacht worden.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32a36ec8-1b36-4677-adfb-431d6b880937",
                                                "sense_id": "e866ef95-cb4c-3f26-9eec-c1bb07c83545",
                                                "text": "„Gleichzeitig versuchte er, einen braunen Mokassin auf den Fuß der Tante mit dem Loch im Strumpf zu schieben.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5127db34-16a2-4e98-8df4-e50a8f8bafa3",
                                                "sense_id": "e866ef95-cb4c-3f26-9eec-c1bb07c83545",
                                                "text": "„Chee stieß mit der Spitze seines Mokassins gegen einen verkohlten Ast.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2059fa2-4eda-4966-b36c-8478cb328a3d",
                                                "sense_id": "e866ef95-cb4c-3f26-9eec-c1bb07c83545",
                                                "text": "„Dann holte er ein Paar Mokassins hervor, die er ständig bei sich trug, und streifte sie über die Füße.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6d9ae77-df50-404f-9785-8ef152bbf6bb",
                                                "sense_id": "e866ef95-cb4c-3f26-9eec-c1bb07c83545",
                                                "text": "„Die Kälte biss ihm in die Beine, als das Wasser ihm die Hose durchtränkte und die Mokassins füllte.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c2e836f2-4790-420b-8738-1fd575b5183e",
                        "source_entry_id": "23ac8405-09c0-3fff-b8a9-7e7c9e7c2aac",
                        "source_sense_id": "d1df6828-d7b7-3b27-b600-38c1b253e74a",
                        "source_sense_description": "een Noord-Amerikaans indianenschoeisel",
                        "target_lang_word": "moccasin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "moccasin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab585930-7dc9-33b9-a69f-5a70c59e3708",
                                        "entry_id": "36db1e4b-c32e-335c-b4c2-be3248d374e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A traditional Native North American shoe, usually without a heel or sole, made of a piece of deerskin or other soft leather turned up at the edges which are either stitched together at the top of the shoe, or sewn to a vamp (a piece covering the top of the foot)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1f06a60-17b9-4bcc-b414-53fc4d567242",
                                                "sense_id": "ab585930-7dc9-33b9-a69f-5a70c59e3708",
                                                "text": "The term Chippewa, which is generally applied to this nation, is derived from that of O̓ˊche̓pe̓ˊwa̓g, which they restrict to the Indians who reside near Fond du Lac, it signifies plaited shoes, from the fashion among those Indians of puckering their moccassins."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85ce778e-3a65-40bd-9d3f-6d90e7c69e9f",
                                                "sense_id": "ab585930-7dc9-33b9-a69f-5a70c59e3708",
                                                "text": "At length Chingachgook turned his eyes slowly towards his son, and demanded— / \"Do the Maquas dare to leave the print of their moccasins in these woods?\" / \"I have been on their trail,\" replied the young Indian, \"and know that they number as many as the fingers of my two hands; but they lie hid like cowards.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92a2ab56-125f-4fd6-826e-3302e46eb127",
                                                "sense_id": "ab585930-7dc9-33b9-a69f-5a70c59e3708",
                                                "text": "The moccasin is preëminently an Indian invention, and one of the highest antiquity. It is true to nature in its adjustment to the foot, beautiful in its materials and finish, and durable as an article of apparel. […] The moccasin is made of one piece of deer skin. It is seamed up at the heel, and also in front, above the foot, leaving the bottom of the moccasin without a seam."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0086e440-d9a3-4536-b1ee-be9e0e6bf0ae",
                                                "sense_id": "ab585930-7dc9-33b9-a69f-5a70c59e3708",
                                                "text": "The carving of the toes, the articulation of which is slightly arched in some cases, shows great delicacy[…]. The feet of the leaping youths of the 'Ivory Deposit' omit this feature, since, as was usual in the sports of the bull-ring, they were shod in mocassin-like gear."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab486520-f160-3a64-8039-5874ca0fd1ba",
                                        "entry_id": "36db1e4b-c32e-335c-b4c2-be3248d374e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A modern shoe with either a low or no heel resembling a traditional Native American moccasin in that the leather forming the sides of the shoe is stitched at the top."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "991efe01-6179-4899-9e8d-99b50f3ecc57",
                                                "sense_id": "ab486520-f160-3a64-8039-5874ca0fd1ba",
                                                "text": "Walking moccasin of gray chrome tanned leather. Waterproof. Flexible elk sole."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b6e54ca-6a0c-40e1-8cd2-13fd8931da2b",
                                                "sense_id": "ab486520-f160-3a64-8039-5874ca0fd1ba",
                                                "text": "The men's shoe, a classic, low-heeled moccasin, was called Model 175. A classier women's version soon followed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4e2b6538-6c66-34bd-a57a-7b3b6435fa5c",
                                        "entry_id": "36db1e4b-c32e-335c-b4c2-be3248d374e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A light beige colour, like that of a moccasin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68b19657-9d33-4ecd-83a0-17b913d37a32",
                                                "sense_id": "4e2b6538-6c66-34bd-a57a-7b3b6435fa5c",
                                                "text": "He came in a primitive, rickety buggy, drawn by an old, moccasin-colored horse, which, it is to be hoped, had seen better days."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53a020d4-0d78-4542-8d53-ea7e5aa51417",
                                                "sense_id": "4e2b6538-6c66-34bd-a57a-7b3b6435fa5c",
                                                "text": "I prefer the Culprit brand in the moccasin color, the red shad color and the black with blue tail."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "18834576-ea41-3f38-880b-33051f02b826",
                                        "entry_id": "36db1e4b-c32e-335c-b4c2-be3248d374e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several North American snakes of the genus Agkistrodon, particularly the copperhead (Agkistrodon contortrix) and the cottonmouth or water moccasin (Agkistrodon piscivorus)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfb097a5-1edb-42b4-bfc0-3b5e4c3693ce",
                                                "sense_id": "18834576-ea41-3f38-880b-33051f02b826",
                                                "text": "The moccaſin ſnake is a large and horrid ſerpent to all appearance, and there are very terrifying ſtories related of him by the inhabitants of the Southern ſtates, where they greatly abound, particularly in Eaſt Florida: that their bite is always incurable, the fleſh for a conſiderable ſpace about the wound rotting to the bone, which then becomes carious, and a general mortification enſues, which infallibly deſtroys the patient; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ef3409e-6b0b-41d8-b51a-91ef69f80e79",
                                                "sense_id": "18834576-ea41-3f38-880b-33051f02b826",
                                                "text": "The excellence of alkaline salts, as antidotes to the venom of serpents, has long been established. The volatile alkali is a common remedy in India for the bite of the cobra copella and viper, &c. The poison of the moccasin and rattlesnake is immediately counteracted by the application of this remedy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c05c24d-eb3d-41a6-a6d4-2b8b0edd5bec",
                                                "sense_id": "18834576-ea41-3f38-880b-33051f02b826",
                                                "text": "Having last considered amphibious reptiles, in treating of snakes we will first describe some of the species that make their home chiefly in the water, among which we find only a single species, the moccasin, that is venomous, and another, the anaconda, that is otherwise formidable."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5b25dde1-58a9-4cf8-bb54-bd416259b999",
                        "source_entry_id": "23ac8405-09c0-3fff-b8a9-7e7c9e7c2aac",
                        "source_sense_id": "d1df6828-d7b7-3b27-b600-38c1b253e74a",
                        "source_sense_description": "een Noord-Amerikaans indianenschoeisel",
                        "target_lang_word": "mocassin",
